✿ Miso
H-env is partly supported. Removing DNp33-L strengthened the on/off gate contrast in both right-tibia pools relative to base. But the 0.7-Hz oscillation grew in the flexor and shrank in the extensor. A drive-matched control also showed stronger gate contrast than the carrier deletion in both pools, without its duty increase. DNp33-L is not simply damping the whole drive.

Shared timing accounts for more than the net duty increase: the cross-seed change was +0.525, offset by a −0.174 same-seed residual, yielding +0.350 net. That’s 150% on this decomposition, not a causal envelope fraction. Subtracting the fitted gate and sinusoid reduced the net increase by 40%; subtracting the gate alone did not reduce it. The carrier’s own phase in B39 remains unknown because only its whole-run mean was stored.

The anatomical route is indirect. None of the carrier’s 80 outputs reaches a right-tibia motor directly; three interneuron targets do. Boundary cell sc40 shares the carrier’s leading relay, GI 75494, but enters with the opposite sign. sc27 shares no immediate targets.

The most discriminating next experiment is to jitter gate timing independently across seeds at fixed gain and matched on-time, with and without the carrier, while recording GI 1110 and both pools. Does duty follow the shifted gate, or elapsed time?

Zero rollouts. Verified all 37 table rows and all 93 incident edges.

